## 15. Mandatory Unified Table Component Architecture (Strict UI Rule)
- Root Table: `<x-table>` (rounded-xl, border, light/dark mode, slots: `toolbar`, `header`, default, `pagination`).
- Table Header: `<x-table.th>` (uppercase font, bold tracking, start alignment, uniform padding).
- Table Row: `<x-table.tr>` (subtle hover state transitions in light and dark modes).
- Table Cell: `<x-table.td>` (uniform typography, responsive alignment, vertical centering).
- Table Empty State: `<x-table.empty>` (centered SVG icon, customizable `colspan`, translated fallback message).
- Table Actions Wrapper: `<x-table.actions>` (`inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 whitespace-nowrap`).
- Table Action Buttons: `<x-table.action>` (polymorphic `<a>` or `<button>` with themes, icons, and tooltips), `<x-table.action-view>` (Indigo/eye), `<x-table.action-edit>` (Amber/pencil), `<x-table.action-delete>` (Rose/trash).
- Strict Prohibition of Ad-Hoc Tables & Action Buttons: Never write raw HTML `<table>` elements or ad-hoc raw buttons with inline SVGs for row operations.

## 16. Mandatory Trilingual Localization Across All Views (Strict Rule)
- Zero Hardcoded Strings: All user-facing text, buttons, labels, and messages in `resources/views/**` and `resources/js/**` must strictly use `__('...')` or `@lang('...')`.
- Complete Trilingual Parity: Every translation key MUST be added and accurately translated into all 3 language files simultaneously:
  - `lang/ar.json` (Arabic)
  - `lang/en.json` (English)
  - `lang/fr.json` (French)
- Zero Missing Keys & Fallbacks: Exact 1-to-1 key parity across all 3 files is strictly required. No English fallbacks in Arabic or French views.
- Pre-Completion Verification: A feature is incomplete until verified that 0 translation keys are missing in any of the 3 languages.

